Azure DocumentDB supports vector-ivf, vector-hnsw, and vector-diskann. You create them via a createIndexes-style command that includes cosmosSearchOptions (or via provider helper APIs). Example form (from Microsoft Learn):
{
  "createIndexes": "<collection_name>",
  "indexes": [
    { "name": "idx", "key": { "path.to.vec": "cosmosSearch" }, "cosmosSearchOptions": { "kind": "vector-hnsw", "dimensions": 1536, ... } }
  ]
}
and queries use $search with the cosmosSearch operator.
